{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b3f2a6b0-2e7e-4c1a-9c1e-switchyard0001",
    "name": "SwitchYard Gateway",
    "description": "Manual/automated coverage for everything SwitchYard supports through Phase 4 (Provider Abstraction, Core Proxy, Streaming Passthrough, Auth & Rate Limiting, Budget Enforcement & Admin API): non-streaming and streaming /v1/chat/completions across all three configured providers, the request-validation error paths, streaming error semantics, the liveness/readiness probes on both listeners, and the admin API for team/provider introspection and live limit/budget management.\n\nBefore running:\n1. Start the gateway with real provider keys loaded (`GROQ_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY` in `.env`) and Redis reachable — rate limiting and budget enforcement both depend on it.\n2. Ollama requests need a local `ollama serve` with the configured model pulled (`ollama pull llama3.2:3b`) — otherwise skip that folder.\n3. Adjust the `*_model` collection variables if your `configs/providers.yaml` lists different model names, and `team_id` if your `configs/teams.yaml` uses different IDs.\n\nStreaming requests: Postman buffers the full SSE body before showing it (it is not a progressive SSE viewer), so you will see every `data: ...` event at once in the response body. For a literal token-by-token demo, use `curl -N` instead — this collection is for correctness checks, not the visual demo.\n\nAdmin API requests target `{{admin_url}}` (port 9090), never `{{base_url}}` — the admin API is deliberately unreachable from the public listener. Running the \"Patch Team\" folder mutates the running gateway's in-memory team registry (not `configs/teams.yaml` on disk); the last request in that folder restores the original values so the collection is safe to re-run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:8080", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "admin_url", "value": "http://localhost:9090", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "groq_model", "value": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "gemini_model", "value": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "ollama_model", "value": "llama3.2:3b", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "team_id", "value": "acme", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Non-Streaming Chat Completions",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Groq - Success",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"object is chat.completion\", () => pm.expect(body.object).to.eql(\"chat.completion\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"choice has content\", () => pm.expect(body.choices[0].message.content).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test(\"usage totals add up\", () => pm.expect(body.usage.total_tokens).to.eql(body.usage.prompt_tokens + body.usage.completion_tokens));",
                  "pm.test(\"request id header present\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"X-Switchyard-Request-Id\")).to.not.be.null);",
                  "pm.test(\"served by groq\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"X-Switchyard-Provider\")).to.eql(\"groq\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"{{groq_model}}\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"Be terse.\" },\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Count from 1 to 5, one number per line.\" }\n  ],\n  \"temperature\": 0.2,\n  \"max_tokens\": 64\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/chat/completions",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "chat", "completions"]
            },
            "description": "Non-streaming completion served by Groq, occupying the OpenAI slot via the openai-compatible adapter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Gemini - Success",
          "event": [
