            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{admin_url}}/admin/reload", "host": ["{{admin_url}}"], "path": ["admin", "reload"] },
            "description": "Re-reads configs/providers.yaml and configs/teams.yaml from disk, validates both fully, and only then atomically swaps them in — a valid reload here is what re-picks-up any hand edits made to either file since boot (including undoing a PATCH from the folder above, since a reload always reflects what's on disk, not prior runtime overrides). The rejected-reload path (a bad YAML file must leave the gateway running on its old config) is intentionally not exercised here — it would mean this collection corrupting your local configs/providers.yaml mid-run. That path is covered by cmd/gateway's own `go test -race ./cmd/gateway/...` (TestReloadRejectedLeavesStoreOnOldConfig), which is safe to run because it never touches the real config files."
          }
        }
